<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="063" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>The first Know-promotion rule: new matter with no budget after 5 days</title>
    <phase>6 Do lane and Briefing fold-in</phase>
    <gate>061, 036 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>One policy row over an existing rule shape.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single policy row using the Existence shape built in task 020.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>061, 036</deps>
    <tags>dataverse,policy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Author the first Know-promotion policy: a new matter with no budget after five days, which is an Absence shape over data Spaarke already holds.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer.</role>
  <goal>A policy row that turns news into work, demonstrating the difference the ontology makes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>A new matter was opened is NEWS; a new matter has no budget is WORK. That difference IS the ontology: membership by rule evaluation, not by recency.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">Dataverse: one sprk_policy plus sprk_policyversion row</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DEFER document-based Absence rules until documents are mirrored. An Absence rule is impossible over reference-mode data, so authoring one now would produce a rule that cannot be true.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this uses the Existence rule type with a notExists clause, the same shape task 021 built. Do not add a new rule type.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Section 0.3 is binding: a capability must TEST what its message CLAIMS. Scope: any sentence, message template or prose this task produces may assert only what the predicate actually read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (reconciliation X-5; FR-26 req 4; FR-49): the version must carry a sprk_decisionplan with at least one action from task 036's catalog, or the rule fails the row contract. WHICH action is not decided (C-19, spec section 11.1 O-12): see escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">AMENDED 2026-10-07: the notExists half reads sprk_budget for the matter. (sprk_matter, sprk_budget) is NOT in PredicateCompiler.VerifiedJoins today (only matter-communication and matter-budget revision), and the writer principal's read depth on sprk_budget is unrecorded. Adding the join is a compiler change with a proof on real data (task 021's standard): see escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">AMENDED 2026-10-07 (D-15): the evaluator skips Restricted and Limited matters for this rule like any other.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Absence rules</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Author the policy row: lane Decide (it is a decision, not assigned work), enabled No until reviewed.</step>
    <step order="2">Author the version with an Existence body: matter created more than five days ago, notExists a budget for that matter.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the message template and verify against section 0.3 that it asserts only what the body reads.</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm it fires on the seeded new matter with no budget, and does not fire on a matter that has one.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="6">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The action the Know-promotion rule offers is not decided (C-19: Assign Work as the recommendation, or a new Create budget executor). STOP and ask the owner before authoring the version.</trigger>
    <trigger>If (sprk_matter, sprk_budget) must be added to VerifiedJoins, or the writer reads sprk_budget at less than organisation depth, STOP: that is a compiler and possibly a privilege change outside this task's scope; ask the owner to schedule it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The Existence rule type and its notExists clause already exist (tasks 020 and 021), and three Do-lane policy rows exist (task 061).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extend: this is one additional policy ROW using the existing rule type and the existing evaluator. No new code and no new rule type.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The Know-to-work promotion is never demonstrated, so the distinction the ontology exists to make (a new matter was opened is news; a new matter has no budget is work) stays a claim in a document rather than a working rule.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">Dataverse: Know-promotion policy and version rows</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a matter created more than five days ago with no budget, when evaluated, then a Signal is produced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a matter of the same age WITH a budget, when evaluated, then no Signal is produced.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the message template, when checked, then it asserts only what the body reads.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no document-based Absence rule was authored.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-33, FR-49. design.md BR-6. Amended 2026-10-07 per reconciliation B.2 row 063 (X-5); C-19 open (O-12).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
